{"id":"overview-components","corpus":"k8s","title":"Kubernetes Components","sourceUrl":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/components/","license":"Kubernetes Documentation © The Kubernetes Authors, licensed CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Kubernetes Components"},{"kind":"p","text":"An overview of the key components that make up a Kubernetes cluster."},{"kind":"p","text":"This page provides a high-level overview of the essential components that make up a Kubernetes cluster."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Core Components"},{"kind":"p","text":"A Kubernetes cluster consists of a control plane and one or more worker nodes. Here's a brief overview of the main components:"},{"kind":"h3","text":"Control Plane Components"},{"kind":"p","text":"Manage the overall state of the cluster:"},{"kind":"p","text":"kube-apiserver"},{"kind":"p","text":"The core component server that exposes the Kubernetes HTTP API."},{"kind":"p","text":"etcd"},{"kind":"p","text":"Consistent and highly-available key value store for all API server data."},{"kind":"p","text":"kube-scheduler"},{"kind":"p","text":"Looks for Pods not yet bound to a node, and assigns each Pod to a suitable node."},{"kind":"p","text":"kube-controller-manager"},{"kind":"p","text":"Runs controllers to implement Kubernetes API behavior."},{"kind":"p","text":"cloud-controller-manager (optional)"},{"kind":"p","text":"Integrates with underlying cloud provider(s)."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Node Components"},{"kind":"p","text":"Run on every node, maintaining running pods and providing the Kubernetes runtime environment:"},{"kind":"p","text":"kubelet"},{"kind":"p","text":"Ensures that Pods are running, including their containers."},{"kind":"p","text":"kube-proxy (optional)"},{"kind":"p","text":"Maintains network rules on nodes to implement Services."},{"kind":"p","text":"Container runtime"},{"kind":"p","text":"Software responsible for running containers. Read Container Runtimes to learn more."},{"kind":"p","text":"Your cluster may require additional software on each node; for example, you might also run systemd on a Linux node to supervise local components."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Addons"},{"kind":"p","text":"Addons extend the functionality of Kubernetes. A few important examples include:"},{"kind":"p","text":"DNS"},{"kind":"p","text":"For cluster-wide DNS resolution."},{"kind":"p","text":"Web UI (Dashboard)"},{"kind":"p","text":"For cluster management via a web interface."},{"kind":"p","text":"Container Resource Monitoring"},{"kind":"p","text":"For collecting and storing container metrics."},{"kind":"p","text":"Cluster-level Logging"},{"kind":"p","text":"For saving container logs to a central log store."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Flexibility in Architecture"},{"kind":"p","text":"Kubernetes allows for flexibility in how these components are deployed and managed. The architecture can be adapted to various needs, from small development environments to large-scale production deployments."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more detailed information about each component and various ways to configure your cluster architecture, see the Cluster Architecture page."}],"lemmas":{"kubernetes":["kubernetes","kubernete"],"components":["component","components"],"overviews":["overview","overviews"],"keys":["key","keys"],"keying":["keying","key"],"keyed":["keyed","key"],"clusters":["cluster","clusters"],"clustering":["clustering","cluster"],"clustered":["clustered","cluster"],"pages":["page","pages"],"paging":["paging","page"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"provided":["provided","provide"],"highs":["high","highs"],"higher":["higher","high"],"highest":["highest","high"],"levels":["level","levels"],"leveled":["leveled","level"],"levelled":["levelled","level"],"leveling":["leveling","level"],"essentials":["essential","essentials"],"cores":["core","cores"],"consists":["consists","consist"],"consisted":["consisted","consist"],"consisting":["consisting","consist